[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124822,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Meyerson naevus is a benign naevus with superimposed spongiotic dermatitis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124823,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8720/0 Meyerson naevus</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124824,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F20.Y &amp; XH8NP4 Other specific types of melanocytic naevus &amp; Meyerson naevus</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124825,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> eczematous naevus.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> halo eczema; halo dermatitis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124826,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124827,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Meyerson naevus occurs predominantly on the trunk and proximal extremities {22699863}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124828,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Erythema and scaling symmetrically surround and extend beyond the borders of the central naevus, producing an eczematous halo. The lesions may be pruritic. Multiple naevi may be involved {20128988}, and similar patterns have been described for atypical naevi and melanomas {31022058; 5580293; 8655726}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124829,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Meyerson naevus typically occurs in young adults, with an equal sex distribution {22699863}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124830,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "<p>The eczematous reaction is probably triggered by factors within the naevus, because excision of the naevus has been reported to lead to regression of the accompanying inflammation {2025942}.</p>\r\n<h5>Genetic susceptibility</h5>\r\n<p>Meyerson naevus may be associated with atopic dermatitis {19706090}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124831,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124832,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124833,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "<p>Meyerson naevus is an acquired, dysplastic, or congenital naevus with superimposed acanthosis, spongiosis, and parakeratosis. Eosinophils may be present.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Halo naevi lack the changes of spongiotic dermatitis and have an infiltrate predominant in CD8-positive lymphocytes, whereas Meyerson naevi show a predominance of CD4-positive T&nbsp;cells {25611257}. Melanoma with associated spongiotic changes can be excluded with close examination of architectural and cytological features.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:34:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124834,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:33:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124835,
